/*
  RecoveryUnlink — privacy pair A green: recovery keys are unlinkable
  across organizations (crib graph://1e005d5c-c11 §9). Bead auto-u8pcx
  (spike: auto-pdvu6). Tracker 8277c76c.

  The per-organization recovery signing key is derived as
  member_recovery_key(code, genesis_id) (idkit/recovery.py) with the
  genesis identifier as derivation context, precisely so one printed
  code never links personas across organizations.

  This is an OBSERVATIONAL-EQUIVALENCE theory, not a trace theory: run
  with `tamarin-prover --diff --prove`. The bi-system gives the
  observer both organizations' ledgers — the genesis ids and both
  recovery PUBLIC keys. LEFT of every diff: ONE printed code produced
  both keys. RIGHT: two independent codes. Equivalence = an observer
  cannot tell which world it is in = unlinkability.

  Calibration: RecoveryUnlinkNoContext.spthy — the same publication
  with the genesis context deleted from the derivation. Equivalence
  MUST be falsified there (the repeated public key IS the cross-org
  link); a twin that verifies is a broken harness, never good news.

  Abstraction: mrk/2 is a free function standing for the
  HKDF-based member_recovery_key; the computational PRF gap is not
  this model's subject (suite convention, crib §5).
*/

theory RecoveryUnlink
begin

builtins: signing

functions: mrk/2

rule Publish_Two_Orgs:
  [ Fr(~code), Fr(~code2), Fr(~g1), Fr(~g2) ]
  -->
  [ Out(~g1), Out(~g2)
  , Out(pk(mrk(~code, ~g1)))
  , Out(pk(mrk(diff(~code, ~code2), ~g2)))
  ]

end
